<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Summa is distributed via Developer ID (not the Mac App Store), so the
	  App Sandbox is not required. We intentionally do not opt in because the
	  app needs:
	    - ScreenCaptureKit access to arbitrary on-screen windows
	    - User-chosen export folders preserved across launches (outside a container)
	    - Writes to ~/Library/Application Support/Summa for the training log

	  Hardened runtime is enabled at the build-settings level
	  (ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME=YES). We request no hardened-runtime exceptions:
	  no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no DYLD environment variables,
	  no disable-library-validation. If we ever need one, add it here with a
	  comment explaining why.
	-->

	<!-- Sign in with Apple: capability code is built and committed, but the
	     entitlement is intentionally left OUT until the "Sign in with Apple"
	     capability is enabled on the App ID (com.josephruocco.ScreenGlossMVP)
	     in the Apple Developer portal. Adding it before then makes the
	     Developer ID export fail to provision. Once the portal capability is
	     on, re-add:
	         <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	         <array><string>Default</string></array>
	     and rebuild with:  ./scripts/release.sh (xcodebuild -allowProvisioningUpdates)
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
